# Cut checks: pictures to look at, not things to keep. Written by
# tools/cut-gunsmith-frame.py every run.
tools/cut-checks/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written by `npm run gen`, built in CI, not committed.
#
# These were committed until now, which put every page of the site on
# raw.githubusercontent.com as well. That host answers /robots.txt with a 404,
# crawlers read that as "crawl everything", and the repo's copy got indexed and
# outranked the real site on GitHub's domain authority. Keeping generated pages
# out of git leaves one copy of each in existence, and the raw URLs 404 —
# which deindexes them faster and more surely than any meta tag on a live page.
#
# Keep in step with what tools/gen-weapon-smith.py writes (the `out / ...`
# calls at the end of main) and what tools/dump-data.ts dumps. The generator
# also records the pages it wrote in data/generated-pages.txt, which the
# workflow checks against.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The pages, as listed in the manifest.
/index.html
/404.html
/attachment/index.html
/ammo/index.html
/smithery/

# Site furniture, written alongside them.
/smith.css
/favicon.svg
/robots.txt
/sitemap.xml
/.nojekyll
/data/generated-pages.txt

# Dumped from src/data/*.ts by tools/dump-data.ts. Everything else under data/
# is an input and stays: weapons.json and ammo.json come from `npm run sync`,
# gunsmith-*.json from the cut tools, scaled-stats.json from tools/scaled.py.
/data/attachments.json
/data/fits.json
/data/rules.json
/data/card-facts.json
/data/uncatalogued.json
/data/weapon-stats.json
